WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
This is a simulated room with eight Wi-Fi sensors on the walls.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:13.000
The white figure is a simulated person. ECHO never sees it. It only sees the radio signals it disturbs.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The violet ring is where the system thinks the person is. It works this out from those signals alone.

4
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
The green points are the parts of the room it believes are occupied.

5
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:38.000
As the person walks the detection follows. The status line shows how far off it is.

6
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Sitting still is harder. A still body disturbs the signal much less than a moving one.

7
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:58.000
The system keeps the person once found. The estimate drifts more though.

8
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Here the person walks behind a partition wall. Radio still passes through it but weaker.

9
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:18.000
The detection still follows with more error near the wall.

10
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:28.000
Now a building with two floors joined by a staircase. Each floor has its own ring of sensors.

11
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:37.000
As the person climbs the ring rises with them. The system estimates height as well as position.

12
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:46.000
The status line says which floor the person is on and which floor the system detected.

13
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Everything here is simulated. Real hardware would need its own testing.
